From: Smartisan ODIN mainline porting effort
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] msm8953: odin: wire up the three physical buttons

The buttons did not behave: volume-up moved the selection the wrong way,
volume-down did nothing at all and the power key did nothing either.

Root cause: lk2nd only consults its device-tree gpio-keys override if the
DT actually has one (lk2nd/device/keys.c, LK2ND_DEVICE_INIT("gpio-keys")).
ODIN's device entry had none, so every lookup fell through to the target
defaults in target/msm8953/init.c:

  volume up   -> GPIO 85                    (works)
  volume down -> pm8x41_resin_status()      (PMIC RESIN)
  power       -> pm8x41_get_pwrkey_is_pressed() (PMIC PON bit0)
  home        -> no fallback at all, always false

The stock device tree settles it. From
arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/u3-p1-msm8953-key-odin.dtsi:

    gpio_keys {
        compatible = "gpio-keys";
        vol_up   { gpios = <&tlmm 85 0x1>; linux,code = <115>; };
        vol_down { gpios = <&tlmm 86 0x1>; linux,code = <114>; };
        key_home { gpios = <&tlmm 87 0x1>; linux,code = <102>; };
    };

  and, crucially, the RESIN PON source is disabled there:

    qcom,pon_2 { qcom,pon-type = <1>; ...; status = "disable"; };

All three buttons are plain TLMM GPIOs, active low. Volume down is *not*
RESIN, and RESIN is explicitly off -- so pm8x41_resin_status() can only
ever read 0, which is exactly why volume-down did nothing.

Fix: add the gpio-keys node with lk2nd,code for GPIO 85/86/87, so the early
return in lk2nd_keys_pressed() is taken and the RESIN path is never used.

Mind the keycode namespace: lk2nd uses its own
(dt-bindings/lk2nd/key-codes.h) -- KEY_VOLUMEUP 0x115, KEY_VOLUMEDOWN
0x116, KEY_HOME 0x122. These are *not* the Linux 115/114/102 from the stock
tree; copying linux,code verbatim would silently map the wrong keys.

On top of that, accept KEY_HOME as a confirm key in the fastboot menu.
Upstream only handles KEY_POWER there, and POWER on this device goes
through the PMIC and is unreliable, whereas the physical Home button is a
plain GPIO that we can already read. This guarantees a working way to
actually pick a menu entry.

Generated against lk2nd 23.1.

---
diff --git a/lk2nd/device/dts/msm8953/msm8953-smartisan-odin.dts b/lk2nd/device/dts/msm8953/msm8953-smartisan-odin.dts
index 690abb3..cffb576 100644
--- a/lk2nd/device/dts/msm8953/msm8953-smartisan-odin.dts
+++ b/lk2nd/device/dts/msm8953/msm8953-smartisan-odin.dts
@@ -16,6 +16,49 @@
 
 	lk2nd,dtb-files = "msm8953-smartisan-odin";
 
+	/*
+	 * 按键：三个实体键全是 GPIO，不是 PMIC 的 PON。
+	 *
+	 * 不加这一段时 lk2nd 会退回 target/msm8953/init.c 的默认实现：
+	 *   - 音量上 = GPIO 85            → 能用
+	 *   - 音量下 = pm8x41_resin_status() 读 PMIC RESIN
+	 *   - 电源   = pm8x41_get_pwrkey_is_pressed() 读 PON bit0
+	 *   - Home   = 根本没有对应的 fallback，恒为未按下
+	 *
+	 * 而原厂设备树
+	 *   arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/u3-p1-msm8953-key-odin.dtsi
+	 * 写得很清楚：这台机器三个键都在 TLMM 上，且原厂**显式 disable 了 RESIN**
+	 * （pon_2 status = "disable"）：
+	 *     vol_up   gpios = <&tlmm 85 0x1>  linux,code = <115>
+	 *     vol_down gpios = <&tlmm 86 0x1>  linux,code = <114>
+	 *     key_home gpios = <&tlmm 87 0x1>  linux,code = <102>
+	 * 所以读 RESIN 必然恒为 0，音量下键必然毫无反应。
+	 *
+	 * 0x1 是 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW（低电平=按下），这里再加 PULL_UP。
+	 *
+	 * 注意键码用 **LK 自己的** 命名空间（dt-bindings/lk2nd/key-codes.h）：
+	 * KEY_VOLUMEUP=0x115 / KEY_VOLUMEDOWN=0x116 / KEY_HOME=0x122，
+	 * 和 Linux 那套 115/114/102 不是一回事，别照抄原厂的 linux,code。
+	 */
+	gpio-keys {
+		compatible = "gpio-keys";
+
+		vol_up {
+			lk2nd,code = <KEY_VOLUMEUP>;
+			gpios = <&tlmm 85 (GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW | GPIO_PULL_UP)>;
+		};
+
+		vol_down {
+			lk2nd,code = <KEY_VOLUMEDOWN>;
+			gpios = <&tlmm 86 (GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW | GPIO_PULL_UP)>;
+		};
+
+		home {
+			lk2nd,code = <KEY_HOME>;
+			gpios = <&tlmm 87 (GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW | GPIO_PULL_UP)>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	panel {
 		compatible = "smartisan,odin-panel", "lk2nd,panel";
 
diff --git a/lk2nd/device/menu/menu.c b/lk2nd/device/menu/menu.c
index 28ab377..6578757 100644
--- a/lk2nd/device/menu/menu.c
+++ b/lk2nd/device/menu/menu.c
@@ -260,7 +260,17 @@ void display_fastboot_menu(void)
 		fbcon_flush();
 
 		switch (wait_key()) {
+		/*
+		 * HOME 与 POWER 都当"确认"。
+		 *
+		 * 上游只认 POWER。但 POWER 在这台机器上走的是 PMIC 的 PON
+		 * （lk2nd/device/keys.c 的 target_powerkey() →
+		 * pm8x41_get_pwrkey_is_pressed()），实测不响应；而机器正面
+		 * 有一颗实体的 Home 键（TLMM GPIO 87，见设备树的 gpio-keys）。
+		 * 给它加上和 POWER 一样的动作，菜单就有一个一定能用的确认键。
+		 */
 		case KEY_POWER:
+		case KEY_HOME:
 			y = y_menu + incr * sel;
 			fbcon_printf_ln(
 				menu_options[sel].color,
